"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th and a phase one budget of $500,000. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research. The team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, including Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing). Key milestones include an idea submission deadline of July 20th for AI-enhanced data visualization, the completion of the testing phase, and the transition to the development phase led by Omar Jensen. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, and a celebration for the testing milestone is scheduled for October 10th."
